140
00:11:35.111 --> 00:11:39.333
then rejects malformed approval.
Insufficient balance returns denial after

141
00:11:39.333 --> 00:11:43.556
two units without mutation occurring. Deep
copying supports local object

142
00:11:43.556 --> 00:11:47.778
isolation, not external non-mutation
claims. Compare trace, receipt, returned

143
00:11:47.778 --> 00:11:52.000
copy, source fixture, and budget together.

144
00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:56.500
Consider an agent searching repeatedly for
one required approval document.

145
00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:01.000
Its first query returns no matching
document or useful evidence.

146
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:05.500
It rewrites wording slightly and receives
the same empty result.

147
00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:10.000
A third proposed search differs
cosmetically but uses identical evidence.

148
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.500
Eight of ten allowed turns have now
already been consumed.

149
00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:19.000
Decide whether the agent should continue,
stop, or change approach.

150
00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:23.500
Name the evidence showing repeated
non-progress rather than mere difficulty.

151
00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:28.000
State what query, result, budget, and
trusted context deserve preservation.

152
00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:32.500
Identify any materially different recovery
that remains explicitly authorized here.

153
00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:37.000
Otherwise, identify the person or role
receiving the handoff next.

154
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:41.500
Explain what uncertainty the handoff must
preserve without guessing resolution.

155
00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:46.000
Remaining budget is a ceiling, not an
instruction to continue.

156
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:50.500
Repetition can waste resources while
creating an illusion of diligence.

157
00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:55.000
Submit your decision and reasoning before
opening the feedback below.

158
00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:59.500
Your answer should mention progress,
evidence, budget, and next ownership.

159
00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:04.000
Do not assume another similar query will
suddenly produce evidence.

160
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:08.235
Stop because recent actions produced no
new evidence or progress.

161
00:14:08.235 --> 00:14:12.471
Remaining turns do not justify cosmetic
variations of failed searches.

162
00:14:12.471 --> 00:14:16.706
Preserve every query, returned result,
trusted state, and spending receipt.

163
00:14:16.706 --> 00:14:20.941
Report precisely that the required
document was not found here.

164
00:14:20.941 --> 00:14:25.176
Do not report that the document does not
exist anywhere.

165
00:14:25.176 --> 00:14:29.412
A materially different source is
acceptable only when explicitly

166
00:14:29.412 --> 00:14:33.647
authorized. Otherwise, hand control to the
named authorized person or

167
00:14:33.647 --> 00:14:37.882
team. Include goal, evidence gap,
attempts, budget, uncertainty, and

168
00:14:37.882 --> 00:14:42.118
requested decision. This record prevents
the next owner from repeating

169
00:14:42.118 --> 00:14:46.353
failed work blindly. If you continued,
distinguish available budget from

170
00:14:46.353 --> 00:14:50.588
evidence-based progress requirements. If
you stopped without preserving searches,

171
00:14:50.588 --> 00:14:54.824
add them to your record. If you omitted
uncertainty, avoid

172
00:14:54.824 --> 00:14:59.059
converting missing evidence into
certainty. Correct recovery protects

173
00:14:59.059 --> 00:15:03.294
resources while keeping future
investigation genuinely possible. The same

174
00:15:03.294 --> 00:15:07.529
principle governs repeated observe-again
proposals in our lab. There, duplicate

175
00:15:07.529 --> 00:15:11.765
canonical proposals stop after five
charged operations total. Stopping is

176
00:15:11.765 --> 00:15:16.000
successful control behavior, not
abandonment of the goal.

177
00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:20.200
Recover from verified state, not from the
agent's narrative. Stop

178
00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:24.400
on denied authority, invalid or stale
state, repeated non-progress, exceeded

179
00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:28.600
budgets, unsafe requests, failed checks,
or unknown consequential outcomes. Persist

180
00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:32.800
a checkpoint containing the run contract
version, safe state references,

181
00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:37.000
completed step identifiers, approvals,
tool results, postcondition evidence, open

182
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:41.200
uncertainties, and next permitted
decisions. Reconcile the real system

183
00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:45.400
before resuming. Classify each step as
verified complete, confirmed failed,

184
00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:49.600
unknown, or unattempted. Resume only after
the checkpoint still matches

185
00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:53.800
current policy, tools, data, and target
state. Compensation and rollback

186
00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:58.000
are new actions with their own authority
and failure modes.

187
00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:02.200
Disable a tool when it exceeds tested
behavior. Transfer control

188
00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:06.400
when the task needs judgment, credentials,
cost, or consequence outside

189
00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:10.600
the run contract. A clean handoff says
what the goal

190
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:14.800
was, what happened, what remains
uncertain, and what decision the

191
00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:19.000
person must make.

192
00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:23.300
Imagine a support agent may approve
refunds below a policy

193
00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:27.600
threshold but finds conflicting order
records. It has read the

194
00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:31.900
case, verified the customer identity, and
made no financial change.

195
00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:36.200
The correct handoff does not say, refund
failed. It states

196
00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:40.500
the goal, identifies the two conflicting
records, lists the checks

197
00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:44.800
already completed, confirms that no refund
was issued, records the

198
00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:49.100
remaining approval and reconciliation
decision, and provides the safe case

199
00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:53.400
reference. The person can resolve the
conflict without repeating identity

200
00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.700
work or guessing whether money moved. A
handoff is a

201
00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:02.000
state contract, not a conversational
apology.

202
00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:06.053
Recovery begins from verified state, never
from persuasive planner narration

203
00:17:06.053 --> 00:17:10.105
alone. Repetition uses a separate fixture
with six steps and

204
00:17:10.105 --> 00:17:14.158
costs. The first cycle charges
observation, proposal evaluation, and

205
00:17:14.158 --> 00:17:18.211
observe-again action. The second charges
observation and proposal evaluation before

206
00:17:18.211 --> 00:17:22.263
duplicate detection. It stops
repeated-non-progress at five steps and

207
00:17:22.263 --> 00:17:26.316
five cost units. No copied or source
ticket field changes

208
00:17:26.316 --> 00:17:30.368
during those observations. BASE cannot
produce this trace because it

209
00:17:30.368 --> 00:17:34.421
permits four steps. The reconciled UNKNOWN
simulation instead permits four

210
00:17:34.421 --> 00:17:38.474
total charged operations exactly.
Observation, proposal, attempted refund,

211
00:17:38.474 --> 00:17:42.526
and reconciliation consume those four
units. Reconciliation observes open

212
00:17:42.526 --> 00:17:46.579
status, balance one-hundred, and version
three locally. This simulation classifies

213
00:17:46.579 --> 00:17:50.632
failed-not-applied and stops without
retrying the action. That local result

214
00:17:50.632 --> 00:17:54.684
never proves what an external integration
would show. With three

215
00:17:54.684 --> 00:17:58.737
